# Task plan: {{ title }}


## Goal

The main winding was of the normal lotus-o-delta type placed in panendermic semi-boloid slots in the stator, every
seventh conductor being connected by a non-reversible tremie pipe to the differential girdlespring on the up-end of
the grammeters.


## Project commands

### Run quality gate

Command:

```shell
make qa
```

Expected output:

All checks pass with zero errors. Test suite reports 100% coverage on modified files.


## Project standards

- [Turbo-encabulator coding standards](docs/standards.md)


## Steps

1. Write a failing test for AC01.
2. Run the test and confirm it fails.
3. Implement the tremie pipe routing logic.
4. Run the test and confirm it passes.
5. Write failing tests for AC02 and AC03.
6. Implement fault handling.
7. Run all tests and confirm they pass.
8. Run `make qa` and confirm no errors.


## Acceptance criteria

- AC01: The tremie pipe accepts well-formed lotus-o-delta input and routes it to the girdlespring within 50ms.
- AC02: The tremie pipe rejects malformed input and returns a non-reversible fault code.
- AC03: The girdlespring remains in its default state when the tremie pipe faults.


## Technical notes

The tremie pipe must be initialized before the girdlespring. Reverse initialization order causes a panendermic fault
that cannot be recovered without a full system restart.
